§ 2542. Renewal of permit [Effective until June 30, 2026].
A permit to operate a pharmaceutical establishment must be renewed biennially in a manner determined by the Division, including the payment of the renewal fee established pursuant to § 2511 of this title.
Code 1935, §  956B;  41 Del. Laws, c. 87, §  3;  24 Del. C. 1953, §  2573;  53 Del. Laws, c. 90, §  30;  62 Del. Laws, c. 251, §§  19, 20;  68 Del. Laws, c. 206, §  1;  76 Del. Laws, c. 167, §  1;

§ 2543. Hearings and appeals to Superior Court [Effective until June 30, 2026].
A person aggrieved by a Board decision made pursuant to this subchapter has the substantive and procedural rights to notice, hearing, and appeal described in § 2531 of this title.
Code 1935, §  956B;  41 Del. Laws, c. 87, §  3;  24 Del. C. 1953, §§  2575, 2576;  68 Del. Laws, c. 206, §  1;  70 Del. Laws, c. 186, §  1;  76 Del. Laws, c. 167, §  1;

§ 2544. Inspections [Effective until June 30, 2026].
Inspections of pharmaceutical establishments are conducted in the same manner as inspections of pharmacies pursuant to § 2534 of this title and, in addition, include the inspection of and activities related to toilet preparations, dentifrices, and cosmetics.
